n":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.7-beta2\n- Not reproducible in 4.6.2\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta2 - Fedora Linux 44 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (nvidia; 595.71.05) - AMD Ryzen 5 7600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 30.42 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you cycle through open scenes with Ctrl+Tab/Ctrl+Shift+Tab, the opened scene will change as expected in the viewport and scene docks, but the selected tab in the tab bar doesn't update.\n\nIf starting on the left-most tab, it may work correctly if you keep cycling in only one direction until wrapping around. After breaking, it remains broken until an editor restart.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/394daf0b-14d3-463b-8fe3-f666d870288f\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n* Open at least two scenes.\n* Press Ctrl+Tab\n* If not immediately reproduced, keep pressing Ctrl+Tab until wrapping around the tab list\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nCan be easily reproduced in any project with at least two scenes.\n\n[scene-cycling-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27775386/scene-cycling-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subsc